 "notes": "Curve digitised from the vector PDF Fig3_ALP_incl_Ebins.pdf in the arXiv e-print (Fig. 3 of the paper): 95% CL upper limit on g_agamma from a->2gamma decays, benchmark 1D global spectral fit of 16-yr INTEGRAL/SPI data, mass range 61 keV - 16 MeV. Axis calibration from tick marks; extraction verified by overlaying on a render and by back-converting to Gamma_2gamma via Eq. (6), which reproduces Fig. 1 (left). Limit assumes ALPs are all of the DM with an NFW Milky Way halo (Karukes et al. 2020: r_s=9.98 kpc, rho_s=2.2e-24 g/cm^3, D=1.289e29 keV/cm^2); it depends on the integrated Galactic D-factor rather than the local DM density (implied local density ~0.45 GeV/cm^3 at the solar radius), so no density rescaling was applied. Masses converted keV -> eV.",
